{#
    The password rules, as static text (TASK-001 Frontend Tasks).

    Mirrors `App\Shared\Domain\Validator\Constraint\PasswordRequirements`. Two of its four rules
    are stated as a live checklist and two are not, deliberately:

      - length and a capital letter can be checked in the browser honestly;
      - the maximum length is not a rule anybody needs to plan around;
      - `NotCompromisedPassword` needs a network call to a third party, so it is described in
        words and enforced only on the server. Reproducing it here would send every keystroke's
        worth of candidate password to an external service from the browser.

    `aria-live="polite"` is on the list, not on each item, so a screen reader hears one settled
    update after typing rather than one per rule per keystroke. `password-hint.js` writes the
    words "met" / "not met yet" into each item, so the state never depends on the colour or the
    tick alone (WCAG 1.4.1).

    The `field` argument is the id of the password input this list describes; the input points at
    `#password-rules` with `aria-describedby`, which is what ties the two together for a screen
    reader.
#}
<ul class="pp-hint-list" id="password-rules" aria-live="polite"
    data-password-hint-for="{{ field }}">
    <li data-password-rule="length">
        At least 8 characters<span class="visually-hidden">, <span data-password-rule-state>not met yet</span></span>
    </li>
    <li data-password-rule="capital">
        At least one capital letter<span class="visually-hidden">, <span data-password-rule-state>not met yet</span></span>
    </li>
    <li>Not a password known to have been leaked — we check this when you save.</li>
</ul>
